ROOT CAUSE (why the fix misses):
  stranded = autoOpened || !Navigator.of(context).canPop()
  On a cold deep-link, autoOpened == false AND canPop() == TRUE — the stack is NOT empty:
  the SPLASH route sits underneath. Get.back() therefore pops onto a dead splash that has
  already consumed its deeplink and never re-navigates.

PROOF THE STACK IS NON-EMPTY: the hardware BACK button on the SAME screen escapes to Home
correctly, via store_screen.dart PopScope's existing branch:
  else if (Get.find<SplashController>().deeplinkRoute != null) -> Get.offAllNamed(initial)
That branch is the condition the failure view's `stranded` is missing.

